AI-EP-001 — HubSpot Contact Property Mapping & Platform Portability

Status: Open (Implementation Correction Required)

Date Added: 2026-07-14

Context

During the BTA Audience Engagement Phase 1 implementation review, inspection of the HubSpot Contact schema identified a mismatch between the BTA domain model and the HubSpot CRM data model.

The BTA Audience capability intentionally captures an Organization because the platform serves multiple audience types, including churches, ministries, faith-based organizations, nonprofit organizations, educational institutions, businesses, and other organizations. "Organization" is therefore the canonical BTA domain term.

HubSpot's standard Contact object, however, does not include a Contact property named organization. Instead, HubSpot provides the standard Contact property Company Name (internal property: company).

Architectural Decision

The BTA domain model remains the system of record for business terminology.

The HubSpot integration layer is responsible for translating BTA domain terminology into HubSpot CRM terminology.

BTA Domain
Organization
        │
        ▼
HubSpot Integration Layer
organization  →  company
        │
        ▼
HubSpot CRM
Company Name

No changes will be made to the BTA domain model or Audience capability solely to accommodate vendor-specific CRM terminology.

Architectural Rationale

This preserves the constitutional separation between:

Domain Model (BTA business language)
Integration Model (vendor translation)
External Platform (HubSpot implementation)

By isolating vendor-specific mappings within the integration layer, the Audience capability remains portable across CRM providers and future infrastructure environments.

Future Cloud Migration Consideration

This decision becomes increasingly important as BTA transitions from the current Fly.io/Vercel deployment model toward AWS-hosted infrastructure.

Maintaining vendor-specific translations within the integration layer ensures:

AWS migration does not require changes to the Audience domain model.
Future CRM replacement (HubSpot, Salesforce, Dynamics, custom CRM, etc.) can be accomplished by modifying only the integration layer.
PostgreSQL remains the governed application persistence layer while HubSpot remains an external CRM service.
Platform portability is preserved by preventing external vendor terminology from leaking into core application models.
Impact
No changes to the Audience frontend.
No changes to AudienceRequest or AudienceResponse.
No changes to Audience Service contracts.
Change limited to hubspot_service.py.
PostgreSQL architecture unaffected.
Supports future AWS migration and long-term platform independence.
Resolution Status

Open — Implement prior to production activation of the Audience capability.
